@@ -10,6 +10,9 @@ ## [Unreleased]
 ### Added
 
 - Database schema and Mermaid diagram in [`docs/database-schema.md`](docs/database-schema.md).
+- Queue management and per-queue call authorization (domain slice): `App\Actions\CreateQueue` (trimmed 1–255 char name, slugified unique-per-entity slug, active by default), `App\Actions\UpdateQueue` (named `name:`/`slug:`/`isActive:` updates, no delete), and `App\Actions\SetQueueAccess` (upsert/revoke per-queue `call` grants on `queue_access`, audit trail `queue.access.granted`/`queue.access.revoked` on the `audit` channel).
+- `queue_access` table migration (FKs cascade on delete, unique per `(entity_membership_id, queue_id)`, JSON `permissions`), `App\Models\QueueAccess` with `QueueAccess::factory()`, and the `App\Enums\QueuePermission` enum (`Call = 'call'`).
+- `App\Policies\QueuePolicy` as the single source of truth for queue authorization: `create`/`update`/`manageAccess` are owner/admin only; `call` is owner/admin always and employee-only with a `call` grant on that queue (corrupted non-array permissions deny). Both call paths enforce it — `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` (every call mode) and `Ticket::call()` (`InactiveQueueException` for inactive queues, then authorization, then the waiting-status rule).
 - Business rules documentation in [`docs/business-rules.md`](docs/business-rules.md): MVP queue management, entity/subscription, roles (admin, owner, employee), tickets, priorities, fairness (3-ticket rule), deterministic call panel, and channels (Flutter totem, web TV, attendant).
 - This changelog (Keep a Changelog).
 - Auth system: Livewire `login`/`register`, password reset and email verification flows and the mail theme — with rate limiting, strict email validation and password rules ([#18](https://github.com/PegaFila/PegaFilaWeb/pull/18), [#19](https://github.com/PegaFila/PegaFilaWeb/pull/19)).
