+### Policy (single source of truth)
+
+Authorization for queue operations lives in `App\Policies\QueuePolicy` and is the single source of truth — actions authorize inside (`Gate::forUser($actor)->authorize(...)`), never through the UI. Abilities:
+
+| Ability | Arguments | Who may |
+| ------- | --------- | ------- |
+| `create` | entity | owner/admin of that entity |
+| `update` | queue | owner/admin of the queue's entity |
+| `manageAccess` | queue | owner/admin of the queue's entity |
+| `call` | queue | owner/admin always; an employee only with a `queue_access` row for **that** queue whose `permissions` contains `call` (a corrupted non-array value denies); everyone else denied |
+
+Both call paths enforce `call`: `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` (after locking the queue and its active check, before mode selection) and `Ticket::call()` (after locking the ticket and the queue's active check, before the waiting-status rule). Non-managers and non-members never write anything. Employees, members of other entities and non-members get `AuthorizationException`.
+
+## Queue Management (owner/admin)
+
+Queues are created, renamed and deactivated by entity managers — **never deleted**; deactivation (`is_active = false`) is how a queue is retired.
+
+| Action | Domain action | Rules |
+| ------ | ------------- | ----- |
+| Create queue | `App\Actions\CreateQueue` | Name is trimmed, 1–255 chars. Slug defaults to `Str::slug(name)` ("Atendimento Geral" → `atendimento-geral`); an explicit slug is slugified too. New queues are active. Slug is unique **within the entity** (the same slug may exist in another entity) — a duplicate (pre-check or unique-index race) is a `ValidationException`, never a raw `QueryException`. |
+| Update queue | `App\Actions\UpdateQueue` | Any combination of `name:`, `slug:`, `isActive:` (`null` = unchanged). Keeping the queue's own slug is fine; taking another queue's slug is a `ValidationException`. |
+| Deactivate queue | — (UpdateQueue with `isActive: false`) | Tickets are preserved; issuing (`IssueTicket`) or calling (`CallNextTicket`/`Ticket::call()`) on it keeps failing with `InactiveQueueException`. |
+| Set queue access | `App\Actions\SetQueueAccess` | Manager sets the permissions of an entity membership on a queue. A non-empty list upserts the `queue_access` row; an empty list revokes (deletes) it. Unknown strings or non-string entries → `ValidationException`, nothing stored. Membership and queue of different entities → `ValidationException`. Non-managers (including an employee granting themselves) → `AuthorizationException`. |
+| Delete queue | — | Not supported. Deactivate instead; tickets must survive. |
+
+**Audit trail:** grants and revokes are logged on the `audit` channel as `queue.access.granted` / `queue.access.revoked`, with context `actor_id` (manager's user id), `queue_id` and `entity_membership_id`. A revoke with no row to delete is not logged.
+
